  GetBlockHash(2) again   -> B2

The two-height-hash check succeeds because B2 itself is stable.

Store.ApplyBlock(B2) then correctly returns:

  store.ErrNonSequentialBlock

because the Store checkpoint is still A1 while B2's parent is B1.

This is NOT a Store corruption/integrity failure.

